      "name": "InitializeConfig",
      "signature": "void InitializeConfig(void * pConfigData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes global configuration state from a configuration data pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read configuration value from input data (at ECX+1 offset)\n2. Store configuration value in global g_ConfigValue\n3. Set global g_ConfigInitialized flag to 1 to mark initialization complete\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npConfigData (ECX register): Pointer to configuration data structure. The function reads a DWORD value at offset +1 bytes from this pointer.\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe offset +1 byte is unusual and may indicate either packed data or unaligned memory access. The actual field being read appears to be at a non-standard offset within the structure.",
