      "name": "CopyStringToBuffers",
      "signature": "void CopyStringToBuffers(char * pSourceString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies a source string to two predefined destination buffers and sets a completion flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment ECX (adjust source pointer)\n2. Scan through source string to find null terminator, calculating string length\n3. Calculate offset deltas for two destination buffers (0x6fa2b1c0 and 0x6fa2ae88)\n4. Copy source string to first buffer (0x6fa2b1c0) byte-by-byte including null terminator\n5. Set up pointer to second buffer and calculate its offset delta from ESI\n6. Copy string starting from calculated offset to second buffer (0x6fa2ae88) including null terminator\n7. Set completion flag at 0x6fa2ae80 to 1 to signal operation completed\n\nParameters:\n  pSourceString (ECX, __fastcall): Pointer to null-terminated source string\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function modifies two global buffers and sets completion flag\n\nStructure Layout:\n  First Destination Buffer: 0x6fa2b1c0\n  Second Destination Buffer: 0x6fa2ae88\n  Completion Flag: 0x6fa2ae80 (set to 1 on completion)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - String length is calculated including the null terminator\n  - Both buffers receive identical string content\n  - ESI register is preserved (saved and restored)\n  - Operation is linear O(n) with single string length scan followed by two copies",
