      "name": "ValidateAndCopyConfigData",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndCopyConfigData(void * pConfigData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates and copies configuration data if the config type matches expected value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load word value from config data at offset +1\n2. Compare against expected config type sentinel (DAT_6fa2aeb4)\n3. If types match, copy 4-byte config value from offset +3 to DAT_6fa2b1c8\n4. If types match, set config ready flag DAT_6fa2b1c4 to 1\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\npConfigData: Pointer to configuration record containing:\n  +0x1: Word - configuration type identifier (compared against DAT_6fa2aeb4)\n  +0x3: Dword - configuration value to copy if type matches\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value; updates global state variables on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If config type doesn't match sentinel value, function returns without modifying globals\n- Used as a validator to ensure only recognized config formats are processed\n- Config type is at offset +1 (word), not offset +0",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
