      "name": "ParsePacketData",
      "signature": "uint ParsePacketData(byte * pPacket, uint maxLength)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Parses and processes a structured packet containing two null-terminated strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load packet identifier at offset +1 and compare against validation key (DAT_6fa2aeb4)\n2. If identifier mismatch, skip to return success\n3. Extract and store packet fields: identifier (+1), data pointer (+3), flags (+7), field at +8\n4. Check special values at offset +8: if -2 set error 0x33, if -1 set error 0x32\n5. Scan first null-terminated string starting at offset +0xe to determine its length\n6. Calculate pointer to second string (after first string and null terminator)\n7. Scan second null-terminated string to determine its length\n8. Copy first string to global buffer at 0x6fa2b04c using calculated offset\n9. Copy second string to global buffer at 0x6fa2b05c using calculated offset\n10. Validate total parsed length against maxLength parameter using CMP/SBB/NEG\n11. Store validation result (1 if valid, 0 if exceeds max) to global at 0x6fa2b030\n12. Return 1 (success status)\n\nParameters:\npPacket (ECX) - byte*: Pointer to packet structure containing identifier, data pointers, and string fields\nmaxLength (EDX) - uint: Maximum allowed length for parsed data\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 (success), validation result stored in global 0x6fa2b030\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Field at offset +8 value -2 triggers error code 0x33\n- Field at offset +8 value -1 triggers error code 0x32\n- String copying includes null terminators\n- Global buffers at 0x6fa2b04c and 0x6fa2b05c must be pre-allocated\n\nStructure Layout (Packet):\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type    Description\n0x1     2     identifier         short   Packet type identifier matched against DAT_6fa2aeb4\n0x3     4     dataPtr            dword   Pointer to packet data\n0x7     1     flags              byte    Packet flags\n0x8     4     specialField       dword   Special value field (-2, -1, or other)\n0xe     var   firstString        char[]  First null-terminated string\n...     var   secondString       char[]  Second null-terminated string",
