      "name": "SignalGameStateUpdated",
      "signature": "int SignalGameStateUpdated(void * pStateData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Signals a game state update event and stores new state data\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract state value from input data structure at offset +1\n2. Store extracted state value in global game state variable (DAT_6fa2b1c8)\n3. Retrieve Windows event handle from global event handle variable (DAT_6fa2b218)\n4. Signal the event to notify waiting threads of state change\n5. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pStateData: Pointer to state data structure containing update information at offset +1\n\nReturns:\n  1 on success (SetEvent always succeeds in this context)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Accesses memory at offset +1 bytes from input pointer (non-standard alignment)\n  - Global event handle (DAT_6fa2b218) must be initialized before calling\n  - Game state variable (DAT_6fa2b1c8) is heavily used throughout game logic (47 xrefs)",
