      "name": "ValidateAndCacheMessagePacket",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndCacheMessagePacket(char * pPacketData, uint nPacketSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates and caches a message packet by copying it to a global buffer and validating its structure.\n\nProcesses two message types (0x17 and 0x19) with different validation and parsing requirements. Type 0x17 is a simple structured message with 4 ushort fields at specific offsets that must all be < 0x100. Type 0x19 is a complex message with the same 4 ushort fields plus variable-length string data that must be parsed. If validation fails or unknown type is encountered, retrieves a human-readable error message via GetReturnAddress and calls CleanupAndAbort before exiting.\n\nParameters:\n- pPacketData (char*): Pointer to source packet data to copy\n- nPacketSize (uint): Size in bytes of the packet data\n\nReturns:\n- void (never returns on error; calls _exit(-1) after cleanup)\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global cache (DAT_6fa2b220) is non-NULL; if so, clean it up and reset to NULL\n2. If nPacketSize is 0, return immediately (empty packet)\n3. Allocate memory (0x227 bytes) for packet cache using AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n4. Copy nPacketSize bytes from pPacketData to cache using DWORD-aligned copy (REP MOVSD) then remaining bytes (REP MOVSB)\n5. Store allocated buffer pointer in DAT_6fa2b220\n6. Read message type byte at offset 0 (CL)\n7. If type is 0x17:\n   a. Validate ushort at offset +1 < 0x100, error 0x233 if >= 0x100\n   b. Validate ushort at offset +3 < 0x100, error 0x234 if >= 0x100\n   c. Validate ushort at offset +5 < 0x100, error 0x235 if >= 0x100\n   d. Validate ushort at offset +7 < 0x100, error 0x236 if >= 0x100\n   e. If all pass, return success\n8. If type is 0x19:\n   a. Validate ushort at offset +1 < 0x100, error 0x242 if >= 0x100\n   b. Validate ushort at offset +3 < 0x100, error 0x243 if >= 0x100\n   c. Validate ushort at offset +5 < 0x100, error 0x244 if >= 0x100\n   d. Validate ushort at offset +7 < 0x100, error 0x245 if >= 0x100\n   e. If all pass, parse variable-length string data:\n      - Load field count from offset +7 (ushort, zero-extended to dword)\n      - Start at offset +9\n      - For each entry in field count: skip 4 bytes, then scan for two null-terminated strings\n   f. Return success\n9. For any other type, error 0x254\n10. On any error: Call GetReturnAddress to convert error code to message, call CleanupAndAbort with error message, exit with _exit(-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty packet (nPacketSize == 0): Early return without allocation\n- Global cache cleanup: Always done first in case previous packet left data\n- Memory allocation failure: Not explicitly checked; if AllocateMemoryWithTracking returns NULL, subsequent validation would fail at first memory access\n- Type 0x19 with zero field count: Loop is skipped (TEST ECX,ECX checks count), returns success\n- Offset validation: All offsets are from cache base; cache is allocated as 0x227 (551 bytes), max offset touched is +9 plus variable string data",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
