      "name": "CopyInitializationStrings",
      "signature": "void CopyInitializationStrings(undefined4 unused_param, char * sourceString1, char * sourceString2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Copies two initialization strings to predefined global buffer locations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate offset from sourceString1 to destination buffer at 0x6fa2b1c0\n2. Loop through sourceString1, copying each byte to destination with calculated offset\n3. Continue until null terminator is copied\n4. Calculate offset from sourceString2 to destination buffer at 0x6fa2ae88\n5. Loop through sourceString2, copying each byte to destination with calculated offset\n6. Continue until null terminator is copied\n7. Store unused_param value to global location 0x6fa2ae80\n8. Return with stdcall cleanup (pop 3 DWORD parameters)\n\nParameters:\n  unused_param: Parameter passed but not used in function logic\n  sourceString1: Pointer to first null-terminated string to copy\n  sourceString2: Pointer to second null-terminated string to copy\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  The function uses offset-based copying (EDX = destination - source) to allow\n  strings to be copied to fixed global locations. The destination addresses\n  0x6fa2b1c0 and 0x6fa2ae88 are hardcoded. If either source string is NULL,\n  the function behavior is undefined.",
