      "name": "ProcessConnectionCommand",
      "signature": "int ProcessConnectionCommand(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes connection command from global connection context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load connection context pointer from DAT_6fa2b028\n2. Return 0 if context pointer is null\n3. Allocate 0x400 byte command buffer on stack\n4. Call ProcessIfValidPointer to read command data into buffer\n5. Validate return value is non-zero\n6. Check command ID (buffer[0]) is in range [0, 0x1a)\n7. Lookup command handler in function pointer table at 0x6fa2a900 using command ID as index\n8. If handler is non-null, invoke the handler via external function at 0x042ac300\n9. Return 1\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global connection context at DAT_6fa2b028\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 if processing completed, 0 if context is invalid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 early if connection context is null\n- Command buffer is 0x400 bytes\n- Command ID must be in range [0, 26) to be valid\n- Handler function pointer table contains 26 entries at 0x6fa2a900\n- Invalid command IDs result in no handler execution but function still returns 1\n\nStructure Layout:\nCommand Buffer Format (0x400 bytes allocated, populated by ProcessIfValidPointer):\nOffset  Size  Field Name       Type       Description\n0x00    0x01  commandId        byte       Command identifier (0-25)\n0x01    0x3FF commandData      byte[0x3FF] Command payload/data",
