      "comment": "Wrapper function that adapts parameters and calls InitializeAndEncodeBuffer with encoding context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load encryption key from stack parameter (ESP+0x8) into EAX\n2. Load buffer pointer from stack parameter (ESP+0x4) into ECX\n3. Push encryption key and buffer pointer as function arguments\n4. Load encoding context value from (ESP+0x14) into ECX\n5. Call InitializeAndEncodeBuffer with the three parameters\n6. Return to caller, cleaning up 12 bytes of stack\n\nParameters:\npBuffer (ESP+0x4): char* - Pointer to source data buffer to encode\nencryptionKey (ESP+0x8): uint - Encryption context key for encoding operations\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns normally; no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This is a __stdcall wrapper that adapts parameter passing to the underlying InitializeAndEncodeBuffer function\n- The encoding context is loaded from ESP+0x14, providing a third implicit parameter\n- RET 0xc cleans up 12 bytes (3 stack parameters) on return",
