      "name": "InitializeEncodingBuffer",
      "signature": "void InitializeEncodingBuffer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the encoding buffer and context for data encoding operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ECX register (caller-saved)\n2. Load pointer from global DAT_6fa2b028 into ECX\n3. Push encoding flag value (0x1)\n4. Calculate stack buffer address relative to ESP\n5. Push buffer address and context pointer\n6. Clear encoding status global flag (DAT_6fa2b1c8 = 0)\n7. Set encoding mode byte to 0x13\n8. Call EncodeBufferWithContext to initialize encoding\n9. Restore ECX and return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nParameters:\nNone - Uses global context pointers\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Encoding mode 0x13 (19 decimal) indicates buffer initialization mode\n- Global DAT_6fa2b1c8 serves as encoding status flag\n- Global DAT_6fa2b028 contains pointer to encoding context structure",
