      "comment": "Encodes a command packet with opcode 0x11 and parameters, then sends it via the encoding context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the encoding context flag at global address 0x6fa2b1c8\n2. Construct a 4-byte command buffer with layout [0x11, commandByte, commandParam (word)]\n3. Pass the buffer to EncodeBufferWithContext for encoding and transmission\n\nParameters:\ncommandByte - The command-specific byte parameter (passed in CL register)\ncommandParam - The command-specific word parameter (passed in DX register)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nStructure Layout:\nCommand Buffer Format (4 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n0       1     opcode        byte    Command opcode value 0x11\n1       1     cmdByte       byte    Command-specific byte parameter\n2       2     cmdParam      word    Command-specific word parameter\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The global at 0x6fa2b1c8 is cleared before encoding, likely a status or flag field\n- The buffer is stack-allocated and passed by reference to EncodeBufferWithContext\n- Uses __fastcall convention with CL and DX registers for performance",
