      "name": "InitializeAndEncodeBuffer",
      "signature": "void InitializeAndEncodeBuffer(char * pSourceBuffer, ushort encryptionKey)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Initializes encoding context with source structure data and encryption key, then encodes buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 1036-byte stack frame for encoding buffer and local variables\n2. Zero global state variable DAT_6fa2b1c8 to clear any prior encoding state\n3. Initialize local buffer size counter to zero\n4. Read 4-byte field from source structure at offset +0x14 into sourceDataField\n5. Set encoding marker byte to 0x5 (version/format identifier)\n6. Store encryption key in global variable DAT_6fa2aeb4 for context\n7. Call FUN_6fa26ec0 to process source buffer, accumulate final size in bufferSize\n8. Calculate total encoding size as (bufferSize + 7) to include header overhead\n9. Call EncodeBufferWithContext with context pointer, marker byte, and total size\n10. Deallocate stack frame and return to caller\n\nParameters:\npSourceBuffer (ECX on entry): char* - Pointer to source data buffer to encode\nencryptionKey (DX on entry): ushort - Encryption context key for encoding operations\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns normally; no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Encoding marker byte 0x5 is a version identifier for this encoding format\n- Header overhead is 7 bytes (marker byte + 6-byte encryption context)\n- Source structure field at +0x14 contains additional encoding context data\n- Uses global encoding context DAT_6fa2b028 for encoder state persistence\n- Stack frame size 0x40c (1036 bytes) allows buffer accumulation during processing\n\nStructure Layout:\nSource Buffer Structure:\nOffset | Size | Field               | Type    | Description\n0x0    | ?    | data                | byte[]  | Source data to encode\n...\n0x14   | 4    | contextField        | uint    | Encoding context data\nTotal size: Minimum 24 bytes (0x18)",
